---
import Base from "../../../layouts/Base.astro";
---

<Base title="Encrypted annexes in Metanorma documents · enprot">
  <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold mb-3">Encrypted annexes in Metanorma documents</h1>
  <p class="text-enprot-muted mb-6">
    enprot's directives live natively in AsciiDoc line comments — Metanorma sources
    can carry confidential annexes that render only at publication time.
  </p>

  <section class="mb-8">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-3">The fit</h2>
    <p>
      Metanorma authors write AsciiDoc; AsciiDoc comments start with <code>//</code> —
      exactly enprot's default left separator. A confidential annex inside a
      specification draft is therefore just a WORD segment in the source file:
      reviewers with the WORD password see and edit the plaintext; everyone else
      sees only ciphertext lines. The published output never contains the annex
      unless the pipeline decrypts it first.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="mb-8">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-3">Source file (document.adoc)</h2>
    <pre class="bg-enprot-ink text-enprot-paper p-4 rounded overflow-x-auto text-sm"><code>= Internal specification

== Scope
This part is public.

// <( BEGIN Confidential )>
Licensing terms for the Q3 partner draft: …
// <( END Confidential )>

== Annex A
Also public.</code></pre>
  </section>

  <section class="mb-8">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-3">Authoring loop</h2>
    <pre class="bg-enprot-ink text-enprot-paper p-4 rounded overflow-x-auto text-sm"><code># encrypt before committing the draft
enprot encrypt -w Confidential -k Confidential=draft-pw --cipher aes-256-gcm-det document.adoc

# reviewers decrypt, edit, re-encrypt (untouched annexes reproduce
# byte-identical ciphertext — diffs stay clean)
enprot decrypt -w Confidential -k Confidential=draft-pw document.adoc</code></pre>
    <p class="mt-3">
      The <code>-det</code> cipher keeps merges and reviews sane: two authors
      editing different annexes produce disjoint diffs, and an untouched annex
      re-encrypts to identical ciphertext.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="mb-8">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-3">Publication pipeline</h2>
    <p class="mb-3">
      CI decrypts with the WORD credential from a secret, renders, and publishes
      the public edition — or renders the redacted edition by skipping decryption.
      The repository's composite action makes this a one-liner:
    </p>
    <pre class="bg-enprot-ink text-enprot-paper p-4 rounded overflow-x-auto text-sm"><code>- uses: engyon/enprot/action@main
  with:
    mode: decrypt
    files: document.adoc
    word: Confidential
    password: ${{ secrets.DRAFT_WORD_PW }}
- run: bundle exec metanorma document.adoc</code></pre>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-3">When NOT to do this</h2>
    <p>
      If the entire document is confidential, keep it out of the public
      repository entirely — enprot's model is <em>mixed</em> documents:
      public structure, confidential regions. Also prefer escrow/rotation
      (<code>--recovery-key</code>) for drafts that outlive any single password.
    </p>
  </section>
</Base>
